<!--
    Objective-C blocks named the way Clang names them, the flags word folded,
    block parameters typed (option objcblocks).

    Issue: a function that builds several blocks and sends each before building
    the next keeps the shared flags word in a callee-saved `d` register loaded
    from a read-only pool, and it read as a load of the pool split across the
    `flags`/`reserved` fields (`block_2.block._8_8_ = v1`, on a
    large app a store back into the pool); invokes were named
    `-[Chain build:]_block_invoke`, a nested one `sum_block_invoke_block_invoke`
    and a global one `block_invoke_<addr>`, none of them the symbol Clang emits;
    a block parameter (`@?`) was `void *`, so calling it read
    `(*((code **)arg2)[2])(arg2,arg1)`.

    Fix: `analyzers/objc/kuna_objcblocks.rs` names each invoke with Clang's
    mangling (`__<len><method>_block_invoke_<n>`, `__<function>_block_invoke`,
    a nested block counted on under the outermost function), a global block
    after the function that references it, the copy/dispose helpers after the
    invoke; types each descriptor; reports the flags pool word constant
    (`ConstGate::ObjcBlocks`); and `@?` decodes to `Block_layout *`.

    Pass 1 (`objcblocks off`): the old names, the split pool load, `void *arg2`.
    Pass 2 (default): `__15-[Chain build:]_block_invoke_2`, `flags = 0xc0000000`
    on the block built after the call, `(*arg2->invoke)(arg2,arg1)`,
    `__sum_block_invoke_2`, `__pick_block_invoke`.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c0035fd6
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
